{
  "source": "edited",
  "logic": "Each case states database rows as in sync/admin-manifest.json (input: now, donors, payments, donations and, where the computation reads them, links and symbolClaims) and, in input.chunks, the rows of every chunk of the administration's device copy the computation reads, keyed <part>/<chunk id> as the device stores them (donations/payments:<yyyy-mm>, donations/donations:<yyyy-mm>, donations/donor-records:<yyyy-mm>, donations/links:<yyyy-mm>, donations/symbol-claims, donations/receipts:<year>, donors/accounts:<yyyy-mm>), with ids aliased as CaseRows names them. The backend runner writes the rows, checks that the sync endpoints answer exactly input.chunks (and input.summary where given), then asks the endpoint for every query of input.queries; the browser runner computes each answer from input.chunks alone. Both compare the whole list of answers with expected.answers. The computation is the donor card of /sprava/darci/<id>, GET /api/admin/donations/donors/{id} in Czech, without its bankAccounts, which stay on the server (whether pairing excludes an account is the server's setting): the donor record as the copy has it; the donor's gifts, newest received first (then the later recordedAt, then the higher id), each with its receipt number (that of the active single receipt of a received gift) or null, the Czech purpose text, the sender account of its bank account link and the confirmed symbol of its symbol claim, whether it is an account verification and whether a receipt is available (received, not an account verification, received in summary.receiptsAvailableFrom or later); the total and count of the received gifts, account verifications included; the donor's receipts, newest issued first, with the day of the gift a single receipt names; yearlyReceiptsAvailableThrough the year before summary.today and receiptsAvailableFrom as the summary names it. Receipts come from the issuer, so these cases hold none; the browser's tests cover them.",
